A||||7||FieroMike||Got it Back!
Z||000000||FieroMike||07-06-99||06:32 AM||||I finally finished getting my engine back together last night!!  I still have a few heat shields to put on and then I am taking it out tonight!!  The car started on the second crank!  Hey Eric, how is yours coming along?<br>Here is the info, any questions?<p>Ported and polished intake and ported exhaust.<br>FM Bearings<br>Crane Comp Cam<br>Chrome Moly Rings<br>High-Volume Oil Pump<br>Power Pulley<br>MSD Blaster Coil<br>New lifters/rods/arms<br>ADS Chip<br>Cold Air induction<br>All new hoses<p>Of course everything is new on the rebuild, but these were the performance mods.  It sounds so nice with the ported exhaust!!<p>I will post some pictures on my website as soon as I get it all organized!!<p>Time to smoke those rice boys.
Z||000001||four50four||07-06-99||02:49 PM||||sounds great! how many ponies do you think you packing now?
Z||000002||Eric||07-06-99||03:19 PM||||I'm ordering my parts this week.  Trying to gather up all my loose change.  I bet you have nearly 180hp.  I'm not sure if the performance of the crane compu cam is as good as the GM performance, but is should be more economical and still provide a solid boost over stock.  Did you get the heads done at a professional shop?  I think it would be a good idea, but I'm also on a budget.  Did you do the manifolds too?  I think I could do the exaust manifolds myself, because it looks easy.  Intake, I don't know.  Is that a big job?  What's involved?<p>Watch out!  FieroMike's coming to get all you 911s.  
Z||000003||FieroMike||07-07-99||11:05 AM||||I was thinking right around 180hp.  As I drive it it keeps getting faster and faster.  It only has 35 miles on it.  The heads I traded in, they were about $100 a piece and they are ported and polished.  The exhaust I did myself with a die-grinder, it is really easy, just time consuming.  The upper intake I took some imperfections off, but I took the mid and lower to Paragon Racing, it was only $35 bucks.  I have a small air-leak that is hissing and my timing is a little off, but other than that it is running really nice, I have got next to many a car that wants to race, but I can't do it until 500 miles at least!!  911's are to slow to race! :-)
Z||000004||Eric||07-07-99||01:31 PM||||Man, that's cheap.  I think I'm going to get raped on the price of the headwork because I really don't know where to take the parts.  FieroMike, did you send out for the heads?  If so, where?  That sounds like a quick and easy solution.  <p>Did you weld the exaust manifolds around the flange?  I heard you can get a leak if you don't.
Z||000005||FieroMike||07-07-99||02:45 PM||||Eric,<br>My local machine shop took my old heads as a trade and they handed me brand new reconditioned ones on the spot for a $100 a piece.  That is the way to go.  I had my dads friend from work weld around the flanges.  All fine and dandy except the the front, left one got bent from the heat and didn't match up to the engine!!  So I still have 1 little tapping noise until I rebolt it on.  Look in the paper for places that trade heads.
Z||000006||four50four||07-09-99||01:59 PM||||hey fieromike if you don't mind me asking how much did you rebuild cost you and where did you get it from?
Z||000007||FieroMike||07-14-99||02:38 PM||||454, sorry about the delay, I actually didn't buy a kit, I purchased the parts seperately from NAPA.<p>Crank (Re-Furb) + Main and Rod Bearings was $160.00, they actually were Clevite 77 bearings.  <br>Timing Set - $48.00<br>Rings - $66.00<br>Hi-Perform Cam and Lifter $180.00<br>Heads were and exchange. $100 a pop<br>Hi-Vol Oil Pump was only $50 for some reason, Fierostore is overpriced...<br>Gaskets - $80 for all gaskets, all-together it was around $720. <br>You could probably do a standard rebuild for $400. With no performance parts.<p>
